[quote="Matchstickman"]

Why? There is still a lowest on the board.If the lowest HP Hero can change within a single card&#39;s damage dealing (e.g. smoke bomb redirecting multiple heroes damage) why can it not happen with villains too?(I don&#39;t know either way, so I am genuinely looking for an answer here)

[/quote]

This is a fair point.&nbsp;

Smoke Bombs might be a different case because the source of the damage has not gone away. The question here I think is whether a Damage Effect can have multiple sources.

Usually, once the &quot;source&quot; of a damage effect has been destroyed, the damage effect is interupted. If a single damage effect (Storm being a single damage effect with multiple instances of damage) can have multiple sources.&nbsp;

[quote="Foote"]

<span style="font-size: 12.727272033691406px;">Usually, once the &quot;source&quot; of a damage effect has been destroyed, the damage effect is interupted.&nbsp; 

[/quote]

I agree with this. Further, usually once the &quot;source&quot; of a damage effect has been determined, it does not change. I can not think of any effect in the game that changes the source of damage dealt.

&nbsp;

So I think that no more damage would be dealt, but I agree that this is not absolutely clear.

&nbsp;

[quote="Ronway"]

&nbsp;
<div class="bb-quote"><b>arenson9 wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">I agree with this. Further, usually once the &quot;source&quot; of a damage effect has been determined, it does not change.
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
Usually the source of damage is listed by name on the card. Or it states &quot;This card&quot;.&nbsp;
<blockquote>I can not think of any effect in the game that changes the source of damage dealt.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</blockquote>
How many cards can you think of that doesn&#39;t specify the source by name or uses &quot;this card&quot;? The Ennead&#39;s one-shots, a few Rook City cards, and Proletariat&#39;s Flanking Maneuvers come to mind.

[/quote]

Captain&#39;s Orders

[quote="Ronway"]

<b>Foote wrote:</b>
<div class="bb-quote"><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">The question still stands though. Can the source of damage change mid-effect?
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
Is the source really changing? Isn&#39;t it the lowest Ennead member who will be doing the damage. If the current lowest Ennead member gets incapped mid damage, is there still a lowest Ennead member still in play? So that means the source is still from the lowest Ennead member.

[/quote]

The effect says the lowest HP villain target deals each hero target damage. If the source changed, say from Atum to Set after hitting the first hero, would Set have to reapply the damage to the first hero? After all, the instructions are still for that singular villain target to hit all heros, and Set would not have done that.&nbsp;

I don&#39;t think either of us would like that interpretation for obvious reasons (maybe I&#39;m wrong there?), but strict reading of the effect instructions like this could lead us down that path if the source of damage effects can change mid-effect.&nbsp;

[quote="Ronway"]

&nbsp;
